# OpenSpec Spec-Driven Development Rules

- Consult `openspec/specs/` before implementing new features or refactors.
- Available OpenSpec skills & commands:
  - `openspec`: Master lifecycle runner
  - `openspec-propose` (`yarn opsx propose <name>`): Scaffolds proposal and delta specs
  - `openspec-apply` (`yarn opsx apply <name>`): Guides implementation following checklist
  - `openspec-sync` (`yarn opsx sync <name>`): Merges delta specs into main domain specs
  - `openspec-archive` (`yarn opsx archive <name>`): Moves completed proposal to archive
  - `openspec-update` (`yarn opsx update`): Refreshes specs and agent configurations
  - `openspec-verify` (`yarn opsx verify`): Validates TypeScript compile and linting
- Implement changes following the spec delta and checklist.
- Verify with `yarn tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit && yarn lint`.
- Archive completed changes and ensure base specs in `openspec/specs/` are updated.
